# QUESTION: Which rules does no computational control check?
# EMPTY: Every rule in AGENTS.md is mechanized by at least one computational control.
#
# READING. A guide is one rule of AGENTS.md. A row is a guide that no computational control
# (a refusal in a tool, a hook, CI, or a program that shapes the work, such as seed's task
# order) says harness:statedBy: the rule exists only as text an agent has to apply. Some rules
# can only be applied by a reader (reproduce before you fix); a row is a candidate for a
# sensor, not a defect. A rule cited only by an INFERENTIAL control (the dispatcher's check, a
# review) is still a row: someone reads, and nothing stops the next miss.
PREFIX harness: <https://ikigai-rs.dev/ns/harness#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
SELECT ?guide ?label ?section WHERE {
  GRAPH <urn:iki:harness:graph:LEDGER> {
    ?guide a harness:Guide ;
           rdfs:label ?label ;
           harness:section ?section .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?control harness:statedBy ?guide ;
               harness:execution harness:computational .
    }
  }
}
ORDER BY ?section ?guide
